(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[12 1 "// The sys module (Python/sysmodule.c; PY5e): made once per interpreter on its first import (sysModule),"] [13 1 "// from the host's configuration (Configure: argv, the search path). sys.modules is the interpreter's"] [14 1 "// Modules, sys.stdout and sys.stderr write to its streams, sys.stdin reads the process's standard input."] [15 1 "// sys.implementation.name is \"arbace\" (PYS15 (a)): Lib/test's @cpython_only tests skip, as on PyPy."] [17 1 "// The host's configuration, set before a run (Configure)."] [23 1 "// Configure sets the next interpreters' sys.argv and sys.path (the script's directory first, then the"] [24 1 "// standard library's Lib), each list's items separated by NUL; bin/pyi's host calls it before RunModule"] [25 1 "// or Repl."] [47 1 "// sysVersion is sys.version: the language's version, then pyi's build in CPython's layout."] [50 1 "// pyVersion315 is the version under REPR_PYTHON_VERSION=3.15 (queue 252): the pin 3.15.2, its Lib on sys.path."] [58 1 "// textFile is a text stream of the process (sys.stdin, sys.stdout, sys.stderr): _io.TextIOWrapper's"] [59 1 "// interface over the interpreter's buffered streams. The rest of io is _pyio's (PY6)."] [63 19 "// what w buffers (writeErr)"] [66 2 "// enc, errs: reconfigure()'s encoding and errors, \"\" the process's (stdioConfig); lineBuf its line_buffering"] [67 2 "// (queue 286: inspect's command line reconfigures sys.stdout's errors)"] [70 2 "// writeThrough: every write flushed, write_through (py-mods-1122: create_stdio's !buffered_stdio, -u or"] [71 2 "// PYTHONUNBUFFERED; libregrtest's --fast-ci adds -u when sys.stdout.write_through is false; reconfigure sets it)"] [75 1 "// stdioUnbuffered is the start's buffered_stdio negated (pylifecycle.c's create_stdio): -u (bin/pyi python's"] [76 1 "// PYI_UNBUFFERED, read once and removed from the environment as PYI_IGNORE_ENV is) or PYTHONUNBUFFERED (not under -E or -I)"] [91 1 "// StdioUnbuffered is stdioUnbuffered for the C API's PyConfig_Get(\"buffered_stdio\") (arbace/pyctypes; py-small-1127:"] [92 1 "// test_regrtest's test_add_python_opts, --fast-ci's -u in the worker)."] [95 1 "// writeErr is a failed write's or flush's OSError (py-eval-1122: with SIGPIPE ignored a closed pipe is EPIPE, a"] [96 1 "// BrokenPipeError, as CPython's BufferedWriter raises it). bufio keeps a write error for every later write and flush, so"] [97 1 "// the buffered bytes are dropped and the writer starts again on what it buffers: json.tool's handler dup2s /dev/null over"] [98 1 "// stdout and exits with EPIPE's status, which the shutdown's flush (status 120 when it fails) leaves."] [109 1 "// encoding is the stream's encoding: reconfigure()'s, else the process's."] [117 1 "// errors is the stream's errors handler: reconfigure()'s, else the process's."] [131 1 "// processStdin is the process's standard input, buffered once for every interpreter."] [150 1 "// ioMethod is a built-in method of t (PY5c's AddMethod: the dictionary filled once str's hash is ready)."] [166 2 "// the standard streams' attributes (PY6b's request: doctest reads sys.stdout.encoding)"] [171 2 "// reconfigure (textio.c's _io_TextIOWrapper_reconfigure_impl; queue 286): encoding and errors (errors \"strict\" when"] [172 2 "// only the encoding is given), line_buffering (a line written flushes), write_through and newline checked; the"] [173 2 "// encoding looked up as the codec registry has it"] [287 2 "// writelines is IOBase's (iobase.c's _io__IOBase_writelines_impl): each line given to the stream's write (queue 574:"] [288 2 "// Tools/patchcheck/reindent.py without arguments writes sys.stdout's lines so, test_reindent's test_noargs)"] [312 4 "// a write error raises (queue 253: flush_std_files reports a failed flush at shutdown, status 120)"] [340 2 "// readlines(hint=-1) and iteration (py-design-1122: json.tool --json-lines reads sys.stdin.readlines()): IOBase's,"] [341 2 "// readline until the end, a positive hint