ns (the references'): the struct sequence of sysmodule.c's flags_desc"] [645 2 "// py-os-1124: -O, -v, -d, -B and their variables (config's optimization_level, verbose, parser_debug, write_bytecode),"] [646 2 "// and hash_randomization as config's use_hash_seed == 0 || hash_seed != 0 (PYTHONHASHSEED=0 without -R: 0)"] [658 47 "// -X int_max_str_digits, PYTHONINTMAXSTRDIGITS (py-eval-1122)"] [661 2 "// -q, -E and -I (queue 296): config's quiet, use_environment and isolated (-I also -E's)"] [671 2 "// -i (queue 289): inspect and interactive; PYTHONINSPECT at start: inspect"] [678 2 "// -X utf8[=0|1] and PYTHONUTF8 (py-mods-1122: 3.14's too, pyi's default 1 kept; test_io's test_text_encoding runs"] [679 2 "// children with -X utf8=0 and -X utf8=1); -X warn_default_encoding and PYTHONWARNDEFAULTENCODING (config's"] [680 2 "// warn_default_encoding, PEP 597: _pyio's text_encoding warns; test_io's test_check_encoding_warning)"] [690 3 "// 3.15's lazy imports (queue 239): sys.flags.lazy_imports, sys.lazy_modules and the mode's and filter's API"] [703 18 "// -X options (queue 220: bin/pyi python passes them in PYI_XOPTIONS)"] [712 2 "// the struct sequences of numbers and threads, with CPython 3.14's values (64-bit Linux)"] [725 2 "// sys.monitoring (PEP 669): its call-family events (queue 220, monitoring.go)"] [729 43 "// PY6c"] [732 2 "// pyi's own launcher when bin/pyi runs it (PY6e: tools/pyi/python3, CPython's command line), so that"] [733 2 "// script_helper and subprocess start pyi as CPython starts itself"] [739 2 "// config's pycache_prefix (py-os-1124, test_cmd_line's test_set_pycache_prefix): -X pycache_prefix=PATH, else"] [740 2 "// PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX (not under -E or -I); -X pycache_prefix with no or an empty PATH none"] [764 3 "// PyErr_SetObject(PyExc_SystemExit, status): a tuple's items are the exception's arguments, None none"] [820 5 "// PyErr_GetExcInfo: the type, the exception, its __traceback__ (queue 223)"] [849 40 "// -1: -X cpu_count unset (os.process_cpu_count from sched_getaffinity)"] [890 53 "// sys__getframe_impl's audit (queue 536)"] [896 2 "// breakpointhook (queue 304): sys_breakpointhook, $PYTHONBREAKPOINT's callable (pdb.set_trace when unset or empty, a"] [897 2 "// no-op for \"0\", a name without a dot builtins'), an unimportable one warned of and ignored; -E and -I ignore the"] [898 2 "// environment (Py_GETENV)"] [922 3 "// PyImport_Import: the leaf module (a non-empty fromlist)"] [940 2 "// the hooks and introspection the stdlib reads at import (PY6a: threading, test.support)"] [946 4 "// _PyErr_Display: the traceback given put on an exception that has none (issue #18776)"] [954 4 "// traceback's display raises for a non-exception; the C fallback's print_exception line (queue 223)"] [963 2 "// is_remote_debug_enabled (queue 223): False, as a CPython built without Py_REMOTE_DEBUG answers (pyi has no"] [964 2 "// remote debugging, :remote-debugging); test_sys imports it at its top"] [1025 3 "// dataclasses' slots=True (gh-135228): __dict__ and __weakref__ taken out of a heap type's dict"] [1043 2 "// get_asyncgen_hooks and set_asyncgen_hooks (sysmodule.c; asyncio's event loops set theirs around run_forever):"] [1044 2 "// the running thread's hooks, a sys.asyncgen_hooks; an argument left out keeps its hook, None clears it"] [1078 2 "// _PySys_SetIntMaxStrDigits: 0 (no limit) or at least 640, sys.flags.int_max_str_digits with it (queue 202: a no-op,"] [1079 2 "// so test_decimal's PyCoverage, which sets 7000, met the 4300 digits' limit)"] [1102 2 "// sys.getprofile and sys.setprofile: the legacy profiler over sys.monitoring (queue 220, monitoring.go)"] [1109 2 "// sys.gettrace and sys.settrace: the legacy tracer over sys.monitoring (queue 219t, trace.go)"] [1136 2 "// threading.settrace_all_threads and setprofile_all_threads: every thread's trace or profile function"] [1179 24 "// its functions' __module__ \"sys\" (PY6f's REQUEST 8, as importBuiltin tags the others)"] [1183 1 "// displayHook is sys.displayhook: None prints nothing; another value's repr is written to sys.stdout and"] [1184 1 "// bound to builtins._ (the REPL's expression statements)."] [1213 1 "// displayUnencodable is sys_displayhook_unencodable (py-os-1124, test_cmd_line's test_displayhook_unencodable): a repr"] [1214 1 "// the stream's encoding cannot encode written encoded with backslashreplace, to the stream's buffer when it has one,"] [1215 1 "// else decoded again and written as text."] [1262 1 "// sysAttr is sys.NAME when the sys module exists and has it, else nil."] [1270 1 "// sysModuleIfAny is the interpreter's sys module once made (interp->sysdict: sys.modules' entry is not needed, queue"] [1271 1 "// 253), else the one in sys.modules, else nil."] [1282 1 "// initSysStreams is pylifecycle.c's init_sys_streams (queue 551, 545-1 (b), the user's decision of 2026-11-23): at"] [1283 1 "// the start, once the import system can import the encodings package, sys.stdin, sys.stdout and sys.stderr (and their"] [1284 1 "// __std*__) become create_stdio's TextIOWrapper(Buffered*(FileIO(fd))) when the interpreter writes to the process's"] [1285 1 "// descriptors; a stream that cannot be made (a closed descriptor) keeps the runtime's textFile, as an interpreter"] [1286 1 "// that writes elsewhere keeps all three."] [1319 1 "// createStdio is pylifecycle.c's create_stdio: _io.open(fd, \"wb\" or \"rb\", buffering, closefd=False), its raw stream"] [1320 1 "// named NAME, under a TextIOWrapper with the process's encoding and errors (stdioConfig), newline \"\\n\", line buffering"] [1321 1 "// for a terminal and for stderr, write_through under -u (no buffer: the raw stream itself), mode \"w\" or \"r\"; nil when"] [1322 1 "// a step fails (the caller keeps its textFile) or when the descriptor is not open (CPython's is_valid_fd: None then,"] [1323 1 "// left to the textFile here)."] [1370 1 "// flushStdObjects is flush_io: sys.stderr's and sys.stdout's flush, errors ignored (the REPL's prompt, input())."] 